// This is a placeholder showing where the real google-services.json
// will live. The real file is generated by Firebase and must NOT be
// committed to git (the project_info inside it identifies the Firebase
// project and would be embarrassing — though not catastrophic — to
// leak publicly).
//
// To enable Android remote push notifications on production EAS builds:
//
//  1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com and create a project
//     named "ToSche" (or reuse the existing Synthera Firebase project
//     if one exists).
//
//  2. Under "Project settings" → "Your apps" → "Add app" → Android:
//       - Android package name: com.synthera.tosche  (must match exactly)
//       - App nickname:         ToSche Android
//       - SHA-1:                leave empty for now (only needed for
//                                Google Sign-In, which we don't ship on
//                                Android)
//
//  3. Firebase auto-enables Cloud Messaging on app creation. No extra
//     config needed for v1 — Expo's push service handles the upstream
//     FCM API on our behalf.
//
//  4. Download the generated google-services.json from the Firebase
//     console → save it as `./google-services.json` at the repo root
//     (alongside this .example file).
//
//  5. Add this line to app.json under "expo.android":
//       "googleServicesFile": "./google-services.json"
//
//  6. Push the change but NOT the JSON file (it's git-ignored).
//
//  7. Next `eas build --platform android --profile production` will
//     bundle the file into the AAB and remote notifications via
//     Expo's push service start working.
//
// Until step 4-6 is done, EAS Android builds still work — they just
// skip the FCM module. Local notifications (the reminders shipped in
// v1.2) continue to work on Android either way.
